cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rvt-rs in academic or archival work, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "rvt-rs: Clean-room Rust reader for Autodesk Revit files"
type: software
version: 0.12.1
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DrunkOnJava/rvt-rs"
url: "https://github.com/DrunkOnJava/rvt-rs"
abstract: >-
  rvt-rs is an open-source, Apache-2.0 toolkit for reading Autodesk
  Revit project, family and template files (.rvt, .rfa, .rte, .rft)
  without Autodesk's software. It reads a file's metadata, preview
  images and embedded schema, and on Revit 2023 to 2025 projects (2026
  experimentally) it recovers the building's elements and exports them
  as IFC4, glTF, plan SVG and CSV schedules, measured against Revit's
  own IFC export of the same models. It comes as command-line tools, a
  Rust library, Python bindings and a browser viewer, is built from
  public observations of the file format, and is not affiliated with
  Autodesk.
keywords:
  - revit
  - rvt
  - rfa
  - bim
  - autodesk
  - ifc
  - file-format
  - parser
  - rust
  - interoperability
  - reverse-engineering
authors:
  - family-names: Long
    given-names: Griffin
    alias: DrunkOnJava
